# TERMS AND CONDITIONS

## 0. Definitions

“This License” refers to the **Open-Astro Public License (OAPL)**.

“Copyright” also means copyright-like laws that apply to other kinds of works.

“The Program” refers to any copyrightable work licensed under this License.  
Each licensee is addressed as “you”. “Licensees” and “recipients” may be individuals or organizations.

“To modify” means to adapt or copy the work in a way requiring copyright permission.  
A “modified version” is the resulting work.

A “covered work” means the unmodified Program or a work based on it.

“To propagate” means to take any action that would make you liable for infringement except running the program.  
Propagation includes distribution, copying, or making it publicly available.

“To convey” means any propagation that enables others to receive copies.

An interactive user interface shows “Appropriate Legal Notices” if it displays:  
1. A copyright notice  
2. A notice that the work provides no warranty  
3. Instructions on how to view a copy of this License.

